      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\n**Missing Kernel Driver Reattachment** In `libusb_transport.cc`, `EnsureOpened()` correctly detaches the active kernel driver using `libusb_detach_kernel_driver`. However, the driver is *never reattached* when the tool exits. For input/fingerprint devices, this means the device will remain dead to the host OS (ChromeOS) until a physical replug or a full system reboot.\n\n* **Remediation:** Track whether the kernel driver was detached (e.g., a `bool kernel_driver_detached_ \u003d false;` member in `LibusbTransport`). In the destructor of `LibusbTransport` (or a dedicated `Close()` method), check this boolean and call `libusb_attach_kernel_driver(handle_.get(), interface_num_)` if it evaluates to `true`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 161,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "52b87cb0d5b393d890281f15a064a751f9d81c13",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
